    {"path":"docs/reference/sdk.md","note":"Reviewed the terminal output section against the committed ccc4eb49021 correction: applyOutput arms the progress deadline only outside ready, keeps the applied cursor and ACK behind the awaited renderer, and still rechecks authority. The new real-session/socket-fixture virtual-time regression failed before the fix (failed instead of ready), then all 26 SDK owner cases passed; a blocked live renderer stays ready beyond six seconds, emits no premature ACK, and acknowledges once after release. Replay remains progress/stall bounded; live rendering is bounded by protocol credit and queue capacity rather than a rendering deadline. Documented operate scope, older-host capability refusal, reconnect limits and native/browser/installed limitations remain unchanged. This is local fixture evidence, not browser or deployed proof.","inputs":["docs/reference/sdk.md","packages/sdk/src/__tests__/terminal-output-session.test.ts","packages/sdk/src/client/terminal-output-session.ts"]},

    {"path":"docs/guides/integrating-station.md","note":"Read the complete guide for the SDK reference delta at ccc4eb49021. Its integration table still directs consumers to the public SDK and requires exact versions, authenticated success and unauthorized refusal; it does not promise a terminal live-render deadline. The SDK now accurately distinguishes bounded replay from live backpressure, without expanding terminal commands, hosted deployment, tenancy, authentication or provider availability. The guide's hosted architecture and dated AWS sizing remain explicitly proposed/historical; those sections are unaffected. No guide prose change or runtime qualification upgrade.","inputs":["docs/guides/integrating-station.md","docs/reference/sdk.md"]},

