    {"path":"docs/architecture/module-map.md","note":"Dispatch-scope test delta review at 7e10b41f70: serviceTier is explicitly classified as Codex routing/billing rather than an approval option. The real mounted routes accept a speed-only request and still refuse approvalMode plus speed for non-operator callers across all six entrypoints. The fixture now supplies a real EventBus and closes its owned Project room store before removing its home, fixing Windows teardown. The documented record ownership, target scope and refusal-before-privileged-hop boundaries remain unchanged. Windows x64 / Node 24.18.0 evidence: 35 cases passed in 155.42s; a temporary serviceTier approval-bypass fault caused exactly six named HTTP matrix assertion failures with 29 passing in 156.34s; the production guard was restored byte for byte and all 35 passed in 180.46s. No production authorization change, live provider, native or remote-Station qualification. This note covers only the changed test inputs.","inputs":["docs/architecture/module-map.md","src-server/runtime/routes/__tests__/runtime-routes-station-control-dispatch-scope.test.ts"]},

