    {"path":"docs/reference/cli.md","note":"Reviewed the dispatch-scope test change at 7e10b41f70 against the CLI's existing model-option and approval-mode explanation and its shared HTTP delegation boundary. Explicit serviceTier classification adds no CLI flag or permission grant; approval overrides retain their existing caller restrictions. Mounted route controls and a known-bad speed/approval bypass exercise the server boundary: 35 passed, six expected matrix failures with 29 passing under injection, then 35 passed after exact source restoration on Windows/Node 24.18.0. The fixture now closes its owned Project room store with a real EventBus. The CLI executable and live providers were not exercised in this delta; no broader CLI qualification is implied.","inputs":["docs/reference/cli.md","src-server/runtime/routes/__tests__/runtime-routes-station-control-dispatch-scope.test.ts"]},

    {"path":"docs/reference/session-api.md","note":"Reviewed existing model-option carriers and caller/approval refusal claims against the 7e10b41f70 dispatch-scope test delta. serviceTier is explicitly reviewed as routing/billing; the four approval options and production guard are unchanged. A speed-only foreground request reaches dispatch, while approvalMode plus speed remains refused across the six mounted entrypoints for non-operator callers. Baseline/restored suites each pass 35 cases; the deliberately bypassed guard causes exactly six HTTP assertion failures with 29 cases passing. Fixture lifecycle uses a real EventBus and closes its owned Project room store on Windows. These checks do not establish live engine execution, billing, release or native behavior; this is a changed-input review.","inputs":["docs/reference/session-api.md","src-server/runtime/routes/__tests__/runtime-routes-station-control-dispatch-scope.test.ts"]},

